! mcp_bootstrap_p223.strap -- MCP printed page 223: the Input Program's
! request scan (V SKIP .. V REQ8, RNMFIL), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.230, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000424  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 223"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224462, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224462.00 to
! 224515.40 (a half word; next word 224516.00), then blank paper.
! The p.222 and p.224 drafts end at 224461.40 and open at 224516.00,
! so the page joins on both sides.
! Remarks run -0434 .. -0477 (octal sequence numbers); rows 29 and
! 41-46 print none, and line 26 prints its -0458 one column to the left.
!
! LABELS.  The names V REQ1 .. V REQ10 print Q with its tail; V REQ10
! is printed "V REQ1C" (lines 35, 40), the open round being 0.
! "V BNCER" (lines 6, 11) is written VBNDER: the glyph has the straight
! left stem and squared corners of the D in V D15 (line 9) and V MD
! (line 26), by the C/D rule -- rests on ink, nothing on this page
! defines it.  "VRQEXT" (line 42) prints the tailed Q of V REQ.
! RNMFIL (lines 41, 46) prints a worn M.
!
! >>> LINE 17 "BZXF" IS BZXH. <<<  The glyph at 900 dpi has a left
! stem and a middle bar, NO top bar (an F's strongest stroke; cf. BXF on
! line 32) and no right stem.  The printed .33 is the indicator of BXH
! (line 11, 224552.33), not of BXF (line 32 .63 = half bit + BXF's .23);
! BZXF would assemble 224475.23.  Settled by binary where ink is a
! broken H/F.
!
! Octal-field opens (".CC", "COCO") are 0.  Hex bytes printed "BO",
! "DO", "CO" are B0, D0, C0.
!
! CARD SERIALS: ?A000424 .. ?A000470; prefix glyph has a straight left
! stem (DA by the C/D rule; the header prints CA000424).  Three pairs
! share a serial: lines 25/26 (448, SIC + B), 42/43 (464), 44/45 (465).
! Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 8 and 29.

